            <ArticleTitle>Atrioventricular 2:1 block as clinical presentation of a septal mass causing left ventricular outflow tract obstruction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S35-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e32833cdd46</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 56-year-old woman with effort angina, dyspnea and a septal mass causing atrioventricular block, treated with pacemaker implantation, and left ventricular outflow tract obstruction (induced by septal mass protrusion into left ventricular cavity).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
